//! The platform a program was built for. These are the target facts of
//! `std/os`, kept here so existing `std/sys` programs still compile.

impl "std/os"

/// The target operating system, as a lowercase name: `"linux"`, `"macos"`,
/// `"windows"`, `"freebsd"`, or `"unknown"`. It is fixed when the program is
/// built, not read from the machine it runs on. Same as `std/os.os`.
fun os() => str = os.os()

/// The target CPU architecture: `"x86_64"`, `"aarch64"`, `"arm"`, `"riscv64"`,
/// `"x86"`, or `"unknown"`. Fixed when the program is built. Same as
/// `std/os.arch`.
fun arch() => str = os.arch()
